1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,560
If I'm going to beg or eat, I'm going to have to tell people.

2
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:10,200
But I can't start with Sylphie. If she breaks down in tears, I'll probably lose my nerve.

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,060
To steal myself, I'll tell Alina Lise first.

4
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:17,800
Correct me if I'm wrong, but I thought I told you to stay put.

5
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,180
Yeah, but I can't.

6
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,080
Okay, fine, if you insist. Shall we go together?

7
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,520
We shall. Thanks, Selina Lise.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,400
I've never been to beg or eat before, but if we take the most straightforward, albeit the most dangerous route, it should take about eight months each way.

9
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,180
That's significantly faster than I'd estimated.

10
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,540
Yay for the wisdom of age!

11
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:52,500
Do not provoke me, Rudeus. The biggest issue I can see will be managing my curse on the road.

12
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:02,580
I'd love to help, but we're not going to be sleeping together.

13
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,640
No, of course not.

14
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:09,780
Couldn't we borrow the magical implement Cliff was making for you? It'll help relieve your symptoms.

15
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:15,180
Well, if I try to take it from him, he's bound to ask why, and then I'll cave and tell him everything.

16
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,320
You're not going to tell him you're leaving?

17
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:20,720
Hmm. Just go talk to the guy.

18
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:23,720
Not about breaking up. About your future.

19
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:27,900
Oh, very well.

20
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:38,420
A 16-month round trip. And if there's trouble in Rippon, it could be more like two years. I'd better start making the rounds.

21
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:45,340
Come in.

22
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:51,480
What's up? I wasn't expecting to see you today.

23
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:56,980
I know. I have some rather unfortunate news to share with you.

24
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,200
Well, go ahead and tell me.

25
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:07,940
I'm leaving school for the labyrinth city of Rippon on Begarit. I figure it'll be two years.

26
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:17,180
That's huge. You're leaving for two years? Really?

27
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:24,740
I know. I promised to help you, and I feel terrible. But listen, I have to make this journey.

28
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:34,900
Two years?

29
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:39,180
Um, I guess I'll be going.

30
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,300
Wait a sec.

31
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,560
Look at this.

32
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:58,360
What is it?

33
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:05,600
A map of ancient ruins, where you'll be able to find teleportation circles.

34
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:06,440
Huh?

35
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:12,080
That page shows you where to find a teleporter here in Sharia that will take you straight to Begarit.

36
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,440
Just like that.

37
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:18,840
I thought... You said you didn't remember where they were!

38
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,480
Yeah, well, that was kind of a lie.

39
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:25,020
I've heard about this Rappan place, though, and I know where it is.

40
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:27,500
Look, see this bazaar near the teleporter?

41
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:31,560
If you travel due north from there, you can reach Rappan in about a month.

42
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:34,020
Just one month? Really?

43
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:37,100
I could make it home before the baby is born.

44
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,360
Keep this to yourself, though, okay?

45
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,840
Teleportation magic is still forbidden.

46
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,560
If word gets out, all those ruins will be destroyed.

47
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,520
Nanohoshi, thank you.

48
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,040
I owe you one.

49
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,760
No, you don't. We're even now.

50
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:56,580
But we do need to keep working, so you'd better hurry up.

51
00:03:58,220 --> 00:03:58,900
I will.

52
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:38,360
I've made up my mind. I'd like to help my parents.

53
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,940
Then you should. I'll take care of things here.

54
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:49,840
I know I promised you I wouldn't disappear. I'm sorry, Sylphie.

55
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:53,360
Don't be sorry. I don't consider this disappearing.

56
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:58,840
But, um, how long will you be gone? Two-ish years?

57
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:07,260
Actually, I talked to Nanohoshi about it, and she showed me where to find some teleportation circles.

58
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,920
So, I should be home before the baby is born.

59
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:15,140
Teleporting? You really think that's safe?

60
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,560
Don't worry. I'll come back in one piece.

61
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:31,500
Okay.

62
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,120
Aisha?

63
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,040
Oh, yes, sir?

64
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,280
Take care of her.

65
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:39,540
Okay, um, I can try.

66
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:45,960
If you run into any trouble, ask for help from people you trust. You don't have to do everything yourself.

67
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:46,520
Okay.

68
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:47,900
And Norn?

69
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:49,860
Yeah? What is it?

70
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:54,580
If these two get overwhelmed, make sure you're there for them, okay? Can you do that?

71
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:55,440
Yes.

72
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:00,900
Oh, and hey, let's pick a name for the baby before I have to go.

73
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:03,040
Um, you want to name the baby?

74
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,760
Rudy, big brother, why would you say something like that?

75
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:07,340
Rudy, yes?

76
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:13,140
They say if you name your baby before a long journey, then you'll never make it back.

77
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:17,300
Oh, are those famous last words in this world? Great.

78
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:18,720
How about this?

79
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:26,300
You can pick a proper name once you're back home, all safe and sound. But if the baby is born before then, we can call them Rudyus Jr.

80
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,900
That sounds good. What do you think, Sylphie? Does that work?

81
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:30,560
Yep.

82
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:41,580
I love you.

83
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:41,640
I love you.

84
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,740
I love you.

85
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:58,720
Once the details were ironed out, I made the rounds with everyone else.

86
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:04,660
I still haven't seen Badi Gadi since that one time at the house. But I'm sure he's fine.

87
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:13,800
I asked Vice Principal Genius for a leave of absence, and got permission to indefinitely borrow books on teleportation and the continent of Begarit.

88
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:15,520
They might come in handy.

89
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:22,520
The plan is this. We'll need to travel about a week from here to the forest where the ruins are located.

90
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:28,000
From there, we'll teleport to Begarit, find the bazaar, and take another month or so to reach Rippon.

91
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:34,960
Then we'll find my folks, bail them out, and hustle back home the same way we came. Perfectly cut and dried.

92
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,080
Last chance. You missing anything?

93
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:46,460
Nope. Got everything that I'll need.

94
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:47,420
Wait.

95
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:47,900
Hmm?

96
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:53,720
It's still far from perfect, but I was able to shrink it a little bit. And it's flexible.

97
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,620
So at least you can wear your clothes over it now.

98
00:08:59,260 --> 00:09:00,340
Take care of Lise.

99
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,040
I will.

100
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:03,700
Oh, Cliff.

101
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:07,460
Lise.

102
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,020
When you get back, let's get married.

103
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,580
I know I haven't broken your curse yet, but I want to build a home with you.

104
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,400
I know I've waited a long time to say that.

105
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,020
You probably started to think I was all talk.

106
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:22,320
Really?

107
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:27,060
But I tried to leave without telling you. I'm a horrible woman.

108
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,380
You don't mind a Mili-style ceremony, do you?

109
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:33,200
I know you're not a follower, but...

110
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,900
Not at all.

111
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:35,920
My darling.

112
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:38,400
I love you more than anyone alive.

113
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:39,860
Rudy.

114
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:42,460
Sylphie.

115
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:45,280
I'll be home soon.

116
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:52,860
Norn, Aisha, you'll be good.

117
00:09:53,380 --> 00:09:57,100
Don't worry. We can take care of everything here. We promise.

118
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,540
Best of luck, brother dearest.

119
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,680
Sylphie?

120
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:08,660
Chin up now. I won't let anything happen to Rudeus.

121
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,560
And we'll be home before that baby arrives.

122
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:14,660
I know. Take care of yourself too, Grandma.

123
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:18,160
Yes, never fear. I am a professional.

124
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,780
Well, we'd better go.

125
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:22,580
We'll miss you.

126
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:22,620
We'll miss you.

127
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:52,300
We'll miss you.

128
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:53,660
We'll miss you.

129
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,300
We'll miss you.

130
00:10:54,300 --> 00:11:24,280
I don't know.

131
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:27,340
I think I found it. This is the stone, right?

132
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:32,140
It matches Nanohoshi's records. I'd say this is it.

133
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:34,660
Purge the barrier.

134
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,900
Lo, the dragon lived only for conviction.

135
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:43,560
Many tried, but none escaped the magnificent reach of his arms.

136
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:48,300
The second dragon to die, the general with the most ephemeral eyes,

137
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,480
the scales of green and silver.

138
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:55,480
In the name of Dragon Emperor Sherrod, I now declare this seal no more.

139
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,300
I've never seen magic like this before.

140
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:16,460
It looks like normal ancient ruins to me.

141
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,420
I'd say this isn't unusual for a labyrinth.

142
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:23,320
Don't be fooled. Keep an eye out for traps just in case.

143
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:23,920
Yes, ma'am.

144
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:27,560
That's suspicious.

145
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,020
Great.

146
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:37,640
I suppose that's the teleportation circle?

147
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:39,560
If I had to guess, yeah.

148
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,100
Let me check real quick.

149
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,600
That's quite a large book.

150
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,100
Exploring the teleporter labyrinth.

151
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:50,080
It's filled with info about teleportation circles.

152
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,600
Some details are different,

153
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,880
but this one definitely has all the signs of a two-way circle.

154
00:12:55,880 --> 00:13:00,780
I found it while Sylphie and I were studying the mass teleportation in Fitoa.

155
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:03,800
I never expected to use it like this, though.

156
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:05,780
One more thing.

157
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,460
We need to be in physical contact when we teleport.

158
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:10,900
Is something wrong?

159
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:11,400
No.

160
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:12,960
It's just,

161
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:15,620
teleportation hasn't been too kind to me.

162
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:17,580
Not sure this will help,

163
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,180
but I know what you mean.

164
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:21,140
You do indeed.

165
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:22,540
Well then,

166
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:23,780
shall we?

167
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:25,220
Let's.

168
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,920
I guess it worked.

169
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:41,280
Looks like it did.

170
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:48,520
Let's check and see if we can make it back to the other side.

171
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,400
I'll go.

172
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,280
You stay here.

173
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,840
If this circle malfunctions and you disappear,

174
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,540
I'd prefer not to have to explain it to Paul.

175
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:56,420
Well, all right.

176
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,460
Mighty kind of you.

177
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:07,380
She's still not back?

178
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:23,340
It worked.

179
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,960
I made it back safe and sound.

180
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:27,020
You were gone for a long time, though.

181
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:27,960
Was I really?

182
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:30,320
I thought I came back after a few seconds.

183
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,540
Maybe there's a time lag.

184
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:33,780
No big deal.

185
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,260
Well, you made it back and that's what matters most.

186
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:49,740
This is it.

187
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,780
Welcome to the scorching desert sands of Bekarite.

188
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:54,800
This place is buried,

189
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,620
but that's not why it's hard to find.

190
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,560
There must be magic hiding it from outside,

191
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,900
though we can see out of it just fine.

192
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:03,420
What now?

193
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:05,920
Should we try and make some headway?

194
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,740
No, it's getting too dark.

195
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,660
We should rest here for the night.

196
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,420
When the sun goes down,

197
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,340
I'm afraid travel will be more difficult.

198
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:14,440
That means the air station would be the same as it cold.

199
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,120
Oh, oh.

200
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:39,220
Oh, oh.

201
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:39,500
Oh, oh, oh.

202
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,080
Oh, oh, oh.

203
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,320
Oh, oh.

204
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:41,720
Oh, oh, oh.

205
00:15:41,720 --> 00:16:04,280
Oh, Cliff.

206
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,700
That was close.

207
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:14,340
I thought I was doing just fine, but I guess I'm more backed up than I realized.

208
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,140
My head's all fuzzy.

209
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:39,560
Luteus!

210
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,560
Luteus!

211
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,560
Keep it in your pants!

212
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:46,000
That's a succubus!

213
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Disgusting.

214
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:53,000
What a foul stench.

215
00:16:53,000 --> 00:17:05,440
Did she hurt you?

216
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,440
Hey, Eulina Lise, come on!

217
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,440
You know?

218
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,440
You've got a really nice body.

219
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,440
It'd be a shame to waste it.

220
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,440
Detoxify yourself, boy.

221
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:20,440
Hey, uh...

222
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,440
Eulina Lise?

223
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,440
I'm...

224
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,440
Sorry.

225
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:26,440
You didn't deserve all that.

226
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,440
You've got a really nice body.

227
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:37,380
You've got a really nice body.

228
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:40,780
Yeah.

229
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:44,480
A pretty nice comun mieć.

230
00:17:44,480 --> 00:18:14,460
We'll be right back.

231
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:32,660
I'll be back. I'm going out for a bit.

232
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,660
Where are you going?

233
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:38,520
A little manhunting. Please don't bother waiting up for me.

234
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,400
Sure, all right.

235
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:46,980
Cliff's magical implement takes the edge off her curse for the most part, but I guess it still needs work.

236
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:51,640
For both our sakes, we better save Zenith soon and get the hell out of here.

237
00:18:51,640 --> 00:19:00,880
Oh, hey, Rudeus. Do you see that up ahead?

238
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:03,200
Let's check it out.

239
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,460
Should we go around?

240
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:11,380
Hell no. Climb on. We're going up and over.

241
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:21,840
Thank you, dear. It's nice to have someone around with so much mana.

242
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:26,480
You can count on me. If there's an easier way, you know I'll find it.

243
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:29,360
Get down!

244
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,820
Two Griffins and two of us.

245
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,920
You deal with that one.

246
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,260
I'm on it.

247
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,420
Come on.

248
00:19:50,420 --> 00:20:17,940
You're not going anywhere!

249
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:32,980
Here you go. Hot and fresh.

250
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:36,840
Thank you, Rudeus. I do love your seasoning.

251
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,740
I am to please.

252
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:45,480
You're a lady, right? Is it so hard to act like one?

253
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:48,880
My word. You're starting to sound just like your mother.

254
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:51,680
My mom used to scold you, too?

255
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:55,620
You're a lady, Alina Lys. Would it kill you to try and act like one?

256
00:20:55,620 --> 00:21:03,340
Come to think of it, if I'm not mistaken, Zenith was about your age when I first met her.

257
